# Repo-wide line-ending rule, set 2026-11-03.
#
# Every text blob is stored LF and checked out LF on every platform. This
# repo sets core.autocrlf=true, which was converting LF blobs to CRLF in a
# Windows working copy: a deploy from this laptop uploaded CRLF HTML while
# the same commit deployed from Linux would upload LF -- identical
# rendering, different Content-Length and ETag on every object. eol=lf
# makes the working copy byte-identical to the blob wherever it is checked
# out, so what you deploy no longer depends on which machine you are on.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Images, fonts and PDFs are never line-ending converted and never diffed
# as text. text=auto already guesses this from NUL bytes; declaring it is
# what stops a guess from being wrong on a file that happens to contain
# none. `binary` is the built-in macro for `-diff -merge -text`.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# SVG is XML, not an image format for these purposes: it stays text so it
# diffs and normalizes like the rest of the source.

# site/tour.html is the canonical record of the bytes served at
# gotovasl.com/tour. Its source is VASL-HEALTH/vasl-platform
# infra/aws/demo-site/content/portal-tour.html, which pins
# `content/*.html -text` for the same reason. Listed last so it wins over
# the `*` rule above: this one file is frozen exactly as stored (LF,
# 22,206 bytes, md5 5728de78989dda2f93c687ee927f1021) and must never be
# converted in either direction, independently of the repo-wide policy.
site/tour.html -text
